  "qualification_complete": false,
  "scope": "Limited manual review of 22 named/hash-verified views from 68 captures. Both assets use exact separately retained diagnostic clips and actual Babylon morph weights. No production motion or appearance qualification.",
  "observations": [
    "At the deep shoulder poses the half-strength target yields 34/17 intersections versus 31/0 for the full corrective, while hips remain 40/27. Both are improvements over the native source shoulder counts 44/35. Both clips reproduce all 16 saved measurements; no browser errors.",
    "Paired oblique and side views show a subtle reduction in shoulder fullness with the half-strength target, but a broad rounded transition and compressed underside remain. The change is not a convincing anatomical improvement sufficient to offset the additional counted contacts. The front detail views are substantially occluded by the raised hands and forearms.",
    "Selected paired 45-degree front views remain broadly similar. Front bind and skeleton views preserve the source silhouette and supported feet. Paired hip oblique views remain similar and still have crease/occlusion limits.",
    "Both GLB exports passed the same validator and preservation checks, and Babylon influence values matched their baked clips. A visually adequate shoulder, residual hip folds, compound/multi-axis movement and real game clips remain unresolved."
  ],
  "decision": "Retain the half-strength result as an unqualified comparison; do not promote it or replace the full-corrective diagnostic. Continue evidence-guided shape repair rather than repeatedly tuning this blend by collision count.",
